-- **`bibliothek/linux` -- the POSIX primitives a HOSTED Gabbro program binds,
-- as ordinary user code** (server lane, TODO section 0e K8, 2026-09-28).
--
-- WHAT THIS IS. Simon's binding constraint (2026-09-27) is *"API calls are
-- always user-made"*, and on 2026-09-28 he drew it for the runtimes too: *"an
-- die Hardware ist OK, OS nicht, das muss selbst gemacht werden"*. So a Gabbro
-- program reaches an operating system only through items IT declares -- with
-- their ABI, their effects, their costs and the assumption their bodies keep --
-- and that now holds for the runtime beside it as well.
--
-- `bibliothek/linux-kmod` is the same file for the Linux KERNEL MODULE target,
-- and it was written first (K7). This one is its hosted twin, deliberately in
-- the same order and with the same three rules, so that the two can be read
-- against each other. **A different operating system gets a different pair of
-- files here, not a different Gabbro.**
--
-- WHAT IT COVERS TODAY, and the boundary is measured rather than asserted.
-- `instrumente/pruefe-os-bindung.sh` reads what the hosted runtime still pulls
-- out of the OS -- `nm -u` over a built binary, intersected with the runtime's
-- own objects, so the program's own calls do not count -- and its mark is the
-- worklist. This file binds the whole of the BOUNDED HEAP
-- (`laufzeit/arena_dyn.c`): the reservation, the commit, the page size, and the
-- two halves of a fail-stop; and, since the second slice, the whole of the
-- GENERATED DRIVER (`<unit>.treiber.c`): its threads, its locks, and the words
-- of its two error paths. **The symbol mark is 0 with these eleven bound** --
-- the hosted runtime names no operating-system function of its own any more.
-- What is left is the raw `clone`/`futex` of `laufzeit/faden.c`, which leaves
-- no symbol at all and is counted as SITES by the instrument's second stage
-- (`MARKE_ROHRUF`).
--
-- WHAT A PROGRAM DOES WITH IT. Two lines in the manifest of a unit that
-- declares an `arena`, a `lock` or a `concurrent` set:
--
--     unit driver program
--       my-program.gab
--       bibliothek/linux/linux.gab   -- these declarations
--       bibliothek/linux/linux.c     -- their bodies
--
-- and `gabbro build` REFUSES a hosted unit that names neither, with the missing
-- declaration and the file that supplies it (`crates/gabbro-cli/src/bau.rs`,
-- `bindungsregel_gehostet`). *Never a silent default* -- and never a link error
-- either, which is what the refusal buys: the linker's word would be
-- `gabbro_os_reserve undefined`, about a name the program never wrote.
--
-- **The demand grows with the use, per thing the unit has**: an `arena` asks for
-- the three storage calls, a `lock` for the three lock calls, a `concurrent` set
-- for the two thread calls, and any of the three for the report channel. A unit
-- with none of them is refused nothing, because the runtime beside it calls
-- nothing.
--
-- **WHY THERE IS NO `use` LINE**, the same answer as the module binding's:
-- nothing in a program CALLS these items, the runtime does. A `use` would name
-- an item the program never mentions again -- ceremony documenting a dependency
-- the manifest already carries. What makes the declarations load-bearing is the
-- pair of checks around them: `gabbro build` refuses a unit that lacks them, and
-- the C compiler holds each one against `laufzeit/bindung.h` inside the
-- runtime's own translation unit, so a wrong type is a build error.
--
-- WHY EVERY ADDRESS IS A `u64`. Gabbro has no pointer type -- the same reason a
-- system-call binding passes registers (Opus agent L, OFFEN O31). The
-- reservation's base crosses as a number and the two sides cast: the runtime
-- with `(uint64_t)(uintptr_t)`, the bodies in `linux.c` back again. Both halves
-- stand beside each other so that neither can drift.
--
-- WHAT THE `costs` CLAUSES SAY, AND WHAT THEY DO NOT. Each one is the
-- primitive's OWN work once it runs. **Waiting is not in it, and neither is the
-- kernel's**: a `mmap` of 32 GiB of `PROT_NONE` walks page tables the program
-- cannot count, and waiting bounds are NOT CLAIMED anyway
-- (`grammatik/Grammatik/Zielsatz/Spec.lean`, the header's list). The numbers
-- below are therefore the same kind of statement as the module binding's -- a
-- declared bound on the call itself, which is what a `costs` clause is about.
module linux::hosted {

-- **The ABI and the behaviour of all six bodies, as one named assumption.** One
-- and not six, because it is one fact about one file: `bibliothek/linux/linux.c`
-- is compiled into the program's own build, with the program's own flags,
-- against the C library of the machine it is built for.
assume os_bindung_abi
    "Every body in `bibliothek/linux/linux.c` keeps the x86_64 SysV convention of its declaration here, answers 0 exactly where the declaration says a refusal is 0, and `gabbro_os_ende` never returns."
    falsifier sonde_os_bindung;

-- **What the thread and lock bodies keep, and it is the whole of what the goal
-- theorem asks of the environment under assumption (d).** A POSIX mutex is a
-- mutual-exclusion lock and `pthread_join` returns after the root's last step;
-- the Lean statement's `Laufzeit` says exactly that about the declared starts
-- and the lock moves, and nothing here re-proves it. It is named apart from the
-- ABI because a binding could keep every calling convention and still hand back
-- a RECURSIVE mutex or a `pthread_create` that ran the body on the calling
-- thread -- both of which type-check, link, and break race freedom in silence.
assume os_bindung_faden
    "`gabbro_os_sperre_nimm`/`_gib` are mutual exclusion over the blob they are given -- at most one thread holds it and a release is visible to the next holder; `gabbro_os_faden_start` runs its root ONCE on a thread of its own and answers non-zero if it did not start; `gabbro_os_faden_warte` returns only after that root's last step."
    falsifier sonde_os_faden;

-- **The three promises the run-time `start` rests on, and their ORDER is the
-- whole of it.** `laufzeit/faden.c` is a LOOP over a join word and nothing else;
-- every step it takes is a reading of this assumption. It is named apart from
-- the pair above because the primitive is a different one -- a raw `clone` and
-- not a `pthread_create` -- and because the middle clause is what was once
-- false: until 2026-09-26 the id was stored AFTER the thread started, a thread
-- that ended first had it cleared before the store, and the join waited forever
-- on a dead one (200000 rounds hung before round 20000).
assume os_bindung_klon
    "`gabbro_os_klon` stores a NONZERO value into the word at `wort` before its new thread can run and clears that word to 0 once the thread has ended, never the other way round; the clear happens-before what a waiter reads; and the root is called with `spitze` as its stack top, ending the THREAD and not the process when it returns."
    falsifier sonde_os_klon;

-- **The reservation reads as zero, and that is its own assumption** -- because
-- the bounded heap does NOT scrub. `laufzeit/arena_dyn.c` commits lazily and
-- stores nothing into a newly committed slot; a program reads a fresh slot and
-- expects zero. That holds for a private anonymous mapping and would not hold
-- for a binding that handed back recycled storage, which is why it is named
-- apart from the ABI: *a binding that reused a freed region would leave a
-- program reading another run's bytes, with every other line of this file
-- unchanged.*
assume os_bindung_null
    "The bytes `gabbro_os_reserve` answers, and every byte `gabbro_os_commit` makes writable, read as zero until the program writes them; a range `gabbro_os_leeren` answered 0 for stays mapped and writable and reads as zero until the program writes it again."
    falsifier sonde_os_null;

-- -- the system calls this binding makes, as GABBRO gates (C-free lane, 2026-09-30) ----
--
-- Until 2026-09-30 the bodies below were C in `linux.c`, over glibc's `mmap`,
-- `mprotect`, `sysconf`, `fprintf` and `_exit`. They are Gabbro now, checked
-- like any user code, and what reaches the kernel is these four gates -- raw
-- system calls under x86_64 Linux's convention, each with the contract it keeps
-- as a named assumption. Their names carry `linux_os_` because the binding is
-- compiled into the PROGRAM's translation unit, and a program may declare a
-- `write` of its own.
pub reason LinuxSpeicherFehler {
    Perm = 1 "the operation is not permitted"
    Again = 11 "the memory is locked or the kernel is out of a resource"
    Nomem = 12 "no memory, or the range is not mapped"
    Acces = 13 "the protection is not allowed on this mapping"
    Inval = 22 "an argument the kernel refuses"
    Overflow = 75 "the range does not fit the address space"
    exhaustive
}

pub reason LinuxSchreibFehler {
    Perm = 1 "the write is not permitted"
    Intr = 4 "interrupted before anything was written"
    Io = 5 "an input/output error"
    BadFd = 9 "the file descriptor is not open for writing"
    Again = 11 "the descriptor is non-blocking and the write would block"
    Fault = 14 "the buffer is outside the process"
    Inval = 22 "the descriptor refuses writes"
    Fbig = 27 "the file would grow past its limit"
    NoSpc = 28 "no space left on the device"
    Pipe = 32 "the reading end is closed"
    exhaustive
}

assume linux_os_mmap_vertrag
    "The Linux x86_64 `mmap` (number 9) with `fd` = -1 and flags MAP_PRIVATE | MAP_ANONYMOUS answers the base of at least `len` bytes of fresh address space, shared with no other mapping of the process, whose bytes read as zero once made readable; or -errno from the listed table; it destroys only rcx and r11."
    falsifier sonde_os_mmap;

assume linux_os_mprotect_vertrag
    "The Linux x86_64 `mprotect` (number 10) over a page-aligned range of a private anonymous mapping makes those bytes readable and writable when `prot` is 3 and answers 0, or -errno from the listed table; it changes no byte and destroys only rcx and r11."
    falsifier sonde_os_mprotect;

assume linux_os_write_vertrag
    "The Linux x86_64 `write` (number 1) reads at most `len` bytes from `buf`, answers the count written or -errno from the listed table, and destroys only rcx and r11."
    falsifier sonde_os_write;

assume linux_os_exit_group_vertrag
    "The Linux x86_64 `exit_group` (number 231) ends every thread of the process with status `code & 255` and never returns to its caller."
    falsifier sonde_os_exit_group;

syscall linux_os_mmap(addr : u64, len : u64, prot : u64, flags : u64, fd : u64, off : u64) -> ptr<normal, rw> u8 or LinuxSpeicherFehler
    abi linux arch x86_64 number 9
    regs in { rdi = addr, rsi = len, rdx = prot, r10 = flags, r8 = fd, r9 = off }
    regs out { rax }
    clobbers { rcx, r11 }
    errors { EPERM => Perm, EAGAIN => Again, ENOMEM => Nomem, EACCES => Acces, EINVAL => Inval, EOVERFLOW => Overflow }
    ensures len <= lenof(result)
    effects { pure }
    costs <= 100000 ops
    assume linux_os_mmap_vertrag falsifier sonde_os_mmap;

syscall linux_os_mprotect(addr : ptr<normal, rw> u8, len : u64, prot : u64) -> u64 or LinuxSpeicherFehler
    abi linux arch x86_64 number 10
    regs in { rdi = addr, rsi = len, rdx = prot }
    regs out { rax }
    clobbers { rcx, r11 }
    errors { EPERM => Perm, EAGAIN => Again, ENOMEM => Nomem, EACCES => Acces, EINVAL => Inval, EOVERFLOW => Overflow }
    requires len <= lenof(addr)
    effects { pure }
    costs <= 100000 ops
    assume linux_os_mprotect_vertrag falsifier sonde_os_mprotect;

syscall linux_os_write(fd : u64, buf : ptr<normal, r> u8, len : u64) -> u64 or LinuxSchreibFehler
    abi linux arch x86_64 number 1
    regs in { rdi = fd, rsi = buf, rdx = len }
    regs out { rax }
    clobbers { rcx, r11 }
    errors { EPERM => Perm, EINTR => Intr, EIO => Io, EBADF => BadFd, EAGAIN => Again, EFAULT => Fault, EINVAL => Inval, EFBIG => Fbig, ENOSPC => NoSpc, EPIPE => Pipe }
    requires len <= lenof(buf)
    effects { reads buf }
    costs <= 64 ops
    assume linux_os_write_vertrag falsifier sonde_os_write;

syscall linux_os_exit_group(code : u64) -> never
    abi linux arch x86_64 number 231
    regs in { rdi = code }
    regs out { rax }
    clobbers { rcx, r11 }
    errors { }
    effects { diverges }
    costs <= 8 ops
    assume linux_os_exit_group_vertrag falsifier sonde_os_exit_group;

-- -- the report channel and the stop -----------------------------------------
--
-- The runtime has no words of its own, because printing is an OS call. A
-- fail-stop travels as a CODE and two numbers (`laufzeit/bindung.h` lists the
-- codes), and this binding writes one sentence per code to the error channel,
-- then the two numbers in decimal -- one `write` per piece, over constant
-- tables, so nothing here is shared writable state and no two threads that
-- report at once can race on it.
pub const LINUX_T_KOPF : [u8; 23] = [103, 97, 98, 98, 114, 111, 58, 32, 114, 117, 110, 116, 105, 109, 101, 32, 114, 101, 112, 111, 114, 116, 32];
pub const LINUX_T_DESKRIPTOR : [u8; 46] = [103, 97, 98, 98, 114, 111, 58, 32, 97, 114, 101, 110, 97, 32, 114, 101, 115, 101, 114, 118, 101, 32, 114, 101, 102, 117, 115, 101, 100, 58, 32, 98, 97, 100, 32, 100, 101, 115, 99, 114, 105, 112, 116, 111, 114, 32];
pub const LINUX_T_SPANNE : [u8; 50] = [103, 97, 98, 98, 114, 111, 58, 32, 97, 114, 101, 110, 97, 32, 114, 101, 115, 101, 114, 118, 101, 32, 114, 101, 102, 117, 115, 101, 100, 58, 32, 116, 104, 101, 32, 115, 112, 97, 110, 32, 111, 118, 101, 114, 102, 108, 111, 119, 115, 32];
pub const LINUX_T_RESERVE : [u8; 46] = [103, 97, 98, 98, 114, 111, 58, 32, 97, 114, 101, 110, 97, 32, 114, 101, 115, 101, 114, 118, 101, 32, 114, 101, 102, 117, 115, 101, 100, 58, 32, 99, 97, 110, 110, 111, 116, 32, 114, 101, 115, 101, 114, 118, 101, 32];
pub const LINUX_T_BODEN : [u8; 55] = [103, 97, 98, 98, 114, 111, 58, 32, 97, 114, 101, 110, 97, 32, 114, 101, 115, 101, 114, 118, 101, 32, 114, 101, 102, 117, 115, 101, 100, 58, 32, 99, 97, 110, 110, 111, 116, 32, 99, 111, 109, 109, 105, 116, 32, 116, 104, 101, 32, 102, 108, 111, 111, 114, 32];
pub const LINUX_T_UEBER_MAX : [u8; 45] = [103, 97, 98, 98, 114, 111, 58, 32, 97, 114, 101, 110, 97, 32, 103, 114, 111, 119, 32, 114, 101, 102, 117, 115, 101, 100, 58, 32, 112, 97, 115, 116, 32, 116, 104, 101, 32, 99, 101, 105, 108, 105, 110, 103, 32];
pub const LINUX_T_SEITE : [u8; 55] = [103, 97, 98, 98, 114, 111, 58, 32, 97, 114, 101, 110, 97, 32, 114, 117, 110, 116, 105, 109, 101, 58, 32, 116, 104, 101, 32, 112, 97, 103, 101, 32, 115, 105, 122, 101, 32, 105, 115, 32, 110, 111, 116, 32, 97, 110, 115, 119, 101, 114, 97, 98, 108, 101, 32];
pub const LINUX_T_START : [u8; 39] = [103, 97, 98, 98, 114, 111, 58, 32, 97, 32, 100, 101, 99, 108, 97, 114, 101, 100, 32, 115, 116, 97, 114, 116, 32, 100, 105, 100, 32, 110, 111, 116, 32, 115, 116, 97, 114, 116, 32];
pub const LINUX_T_WARTE : [u8; 38] = [103, 97, 98, 98, 114, 111, 58, 32, 97, 32, 115, 116, 97, 114, 116, 101, 100, 32, 114, 111, 111, 116, 32, 119, 97, 115, 32, 110, 111, 116, 32, 106, 111, 105, 110, 101, 100, 32];
pub const LINUX_T_AUF : [u8; 1] = [40];
pub const LINUX_T_KOMMA : [u8; 2] = [44, 32];
pub const LINUX_T_ZU : [u8; 2] = [41, 10];
pub const LINUX_Z0 : [u8; 1] = [48];
pub const LINUX_Z1 : [u8; 1] = [49];
pub const LINUX_Z2 : [u8; 1] = [50];
pub const LINUX_Z3 : [u8; 1] = [51];
pub const LINUX_Z4 : [u8; 1] = [52];
pub const LINUX_Z5 : [u8; 1] = [53];
pub const LINUX_Z6 : [u8; 1] = [54];
pub const LINUX_Z7 : [u8; 1] = [55];
pub const LINUX_Z8 : [u8; 1] = [56];
pub const LINUX_Z9 : [u8; 1] = [57];

fn linux_os_ziffer(d : u64 in 0 .. 9)
    effects { reads LINUX_Z0, reads LINUX_Z1, reads LINUX_Z2, reads LINUX_Z3, reads LINUX_Z4, reads LINUX_Z5, reads LINUX_Z6, reads LINUX_Z7, reads LINUX_Z8, reads LINUX_Z9 }
    costs <= 200 ops
{
    if d == 0 {
        let n = linux_os_write(2, LINUX_Z0, 1) else (e) { return; }
    } else if d == 1 {
        let n = linux_os_write(2, LINUX_Z1, 1) else (e) { return; }
    } else if d == 2 {
        let n = linux_os_write(2, LINUX_Z2, 1) else (e) { return; }
    } else if d == 3 {
        let n = linux_os_write(2, LINUX_Z3, 1) else (e) { return; }
    } else if d == 4 {
        let n = linux_os_write(2, LINUX_Z4, 1) else (e) { return; }
    } else if d == 5 {
        let n = linux_os_write(2, LINUX_Z5, 1) else (e) { return; }
    } else if d == 6 {
        let n = linux_os_write(2, LINUX_Z6, 1) else (e) { return; }
    } else if d == 7 {
        let n = linux_os_write(2, LINUX_Z7, 1) else (e) { return; }
    } else if d == 8 {
        let n = linux_os_write(2, LINUX_Z8, 1) else (e) { return; }
    } else if d == 9 {
        let n = linux_os_write(2, LINUX_Z9, 1) else (e) { return; }
    }
}

-- The decimal digits of `v`, most significant first, no leading zeros.
fn linux_os_zahl(v : u64)
    effects { reads LINUX_Z0, reads LINUX_Z1, reads LINUX_Z2, reads LINUX_Z3, reads LINUX_Z4, reads LINUX_Z5, reads LINUX_Z6, reads LINUX_Z7, reads LINUX_Z8, reads LINUX_Z9 }
    costs <= 8000 ops
{
    let mut stelle : u64 = 10000000000000000000;
    let mut begonnen : bool = false;
    retry stellen until stelle == 0
        bounded 6000 ops
        on_exceeded gabbro_os_haengt
        effects { reads LINUX_Z0, reads LINUX_Z1, reads LINUX_Z2, reads LINUX_Z3, reads LINUX_Z4, reads LINUX_Z5, reads LINUX_Z6, reads LINUX_Z7, reads LINUX_Z8, reads LINUX_Z9 }
    {
        narrow stelle to 1 .. 10000000000000000000 else { return; }
        let d = (v / stelle) % 10;
        if d != 0 || begonnen || stelle == 1 {
            linux_os_ziffer(d);
            begonnen = true;
        }
        stelle = stelle / 10;
    }
}

pub fn gabbro_os_melden(code : u32, a : u64, b : u64)
    effects { reads LINUX_T_KOPF, reads LINUX_T_DESKRIPTOR, reads LINUX_T_SPANNE, reads LINUX_T_RESERVE, reads LINUX_T_BODEN, reads LINUX_T_UEBER_MAX, reads LINUX_T_SEITE, reads LINUX_T_START, reads LINUX_T_WARTE, reads LINUX_T_AUF, reads LINUX_T_KOMMA, reads LINUX_T_ZU, reads LINUX_Z0, reads LINUX_Z1, reads LINUX_Z2, reads LINUX_Z3, reads LINUX_Z4, reads LINUX_Z5, reads LINUX_Z6, reads LINUX_Z7, reads LINUX_Z8, reads LINUX_Z9 }
    costs <= 20000 ops
{
    if code == 1 {
        let n1 = linux_os_write(2, LINUX_T_DESKRIPTOR, 46) else (e) { return; }
    } else if code == 2 {
        let n2 = linux_os_write(2, LINUX_T_SPANNE, 50) else (e) { return; }
    } else if code == 3 {
        let n3 = linux_os_write(2, LINUX_T_RESERVE, 46) else (e) { return; }
    } else if code == 4 {
        let n4 = linux_os_write(2, LINUX_T_BODEN, 55) else (e) { return; }
    } else if code == 5 {
        let n5 = linux_os_write(2, LINUX_T_UEBER_MAX, 45) else (e) { return; }
    } else if code == 6 {
        let n6 = linux_os_write(2, LINUX_T_SEITE, 55) else (e) { return; }
    } else if code == 7 {
        let n7 = linux_os_write(2, LINUX_T_START, 39) else (e) { return; }
    } else if code == 8 {
        let n8 = linux_os_write(2, LINUX_T_WARTE, 38) else (e) { return; }
    } else {
        let n9 = linux_os_write(2, LINUX_T_KOPF, 23) else (e) { return; }
    }
    let n10 = linux_os_write(2, LINUX_T_AUF, 1) else (e) { return; }
    linux_os_zahl(a);
    let n11 = linux_os_write(2, LINUX_T_KOMMA, 2) else (e) { return; }
    linux_os_zahl(b);
    let n12 = linux_os_write(2, LINUX_T_ZU, 2) else (e) { return; }
}

-- `gabbro_os_ende` NEVER RETURNS, and since 2026-09-30 Gabbro says so: it is a
-- `-> never` function over the `exit_group` gate.
pub fn gabbro_os_ende(code : u32) -> never
    effects { diverges }
    costs <= 16 ops
{
    linux_os_exit_group(code);
}

-- The stop of a bounded loop that ran past its bound -- which the bound's own
-- check says cannot happen; `abort()`'s status, without `abort()`.
fn gabbro_os_haengt() -> never
    effects { diverges }
    costs <= 16 ops
{
    linux_os_exit_group(134);
}

-- -- the bounded heap's storage ----------------------------------------------
--
-- `reserve` answers a REGION of `bytes` of reserved-but-not-committed address
-- space (`PROT_NONE`), and never 0: a refused reservation ends the process here,
-- because at load no program runs that could take an `else`. `commit` makes the
-- `bytes` from `stelle` on readable and writable and answers 0 on success.
-- `seitengroesse` is the granularity the runtime rounds to -- x86_64 Linux's
-- base page, a fact about this binding's target. The ceiling, the committed
-- prefix and refuse-on-full are the runtime's arithmetic (the generated arena
-- runtime, template `arena.dyn`), and the binding never decides where a page
-- begins.
pub fn gabbro_os_reserve(bytes : u64) -> ptr<normal, rw> u8
    effects { diverges, reads LINUX_T_KOPF, reads LINUX_T_DESKRIPTOR, reads LINUX_T_SPANNE, reads LINUX_T_RESERVE, reads LINUX_T_BODEN, reads LINUX_T_UEBER_MAX, reads LINUX_T_SEITE, reads LINUX_T_START, reads LINUX_T_WARTE, reads LINUX_T_AUF, reads LINUX_T_KOMMA, reads LINUX_T_ZU, reads LINUX_Z0, reads LINUX_Z1, reads LINUX_Z2, reads LINUX_Z3, reads LINUX_Z4, reads LINUX_Z5, reads LINUX_Z6, reads LINUX_Z7, reads LINUX_Z8, reads LINUX_Z9 }
    costs <= 200000 ops
{
    let r = linux_os_mmap(0, bytes, 0, 34, 18446744073709551615, 0) else (e) {
        gabbro_os_melden(3, bytes, 0);
        gabbro_os_ende(3);
    }
    return r;
}

pub fn gabbro_os_commit(stelle : ptr<normal, rw> u8, bytes : u64) -> u32
    requires bytes <= lenof(stelle)
    effects { pure }
    costs <= 100016 ops
{
    let x = linux_os_mprotect(stelle, bytes, 3) else (e) { return 1; }
    return 0;
}

pub fn gabbro_os_seitengroesse() -> u64
    effects { pure }
    costs <= 4 ops
{
    return 4096;
}

-- `leeren` is the way back (M-ALLTAG C): the bytes at `addr` read as zero
-- afterwards and the whole pages inside them went back to the system; answers
-- 0 when it kept that promise. The range stays mapped and writable
-- (`os_bindung_null` names the promise). Only a unit that writes
-- `reset X at i count n;` gains from it; a unit that does not bind it gets the
-- same zeroes from the emitted loop, without the page return.
extern fn gabbro_os_leeren(addr : u64, bytes : u64) -> u32
    effects { pure } costs <= 100000 ops;

-- -- the generated driver's locks ---------------------------------------------
--
-- One blob per `lock`, owned by `<unit>.treiber.c` and passed as a number. The
-- driver takes and releases; the binding decides with WHAT, and fail-stops
-- itself if the primitive refuses -- there is no `else` at a lock the driver
-- must hold, and the words are on this side anyway.
--
-- **The `costs` is the primitive's own work and NOT the wait.** `held <= N ops`
-- is the Gabbro clause that bounds a critical section, and waiting bounds are
-- NOT CLAIMED (`grammatik/Grammatik/Zielsatz/Spec.lean`, the header's list). A
-- number here that pretended to cover contention would be the one kind of cost
-- clause this language refuses to write.
extern fn gabbro_os_sperre_init(s : u64)
    effects { pure } costs <= 4096 ops;

extern fn gabbro_os_sperre_nimm(s : u64)
    effects { pure } costs <= 4096 ops;

extern fn gabbro_os_sperre_gib(s : u64)
    effects { pure } costs <= 4096 ops;

-- -- the generated driver's threads -------------------------------------------
--
-- `start` takes the blob and the address of the root and answers 0 or an error;
-- `warte` joins it. The body owns the whole lifecycle, which is why a FAILED
-- start must leave a blob the driver may still wait on: the driver's error path
-- joins everything it started before the failure, and a blob that never
-- completed would hang the program instead of ending it with status 2.
extern fn gabbro_os_faden_start(f : u64, koerper : u64) -> u32
    effects { pure } costs <= 100000 ops;

extern fn gabbro_os_faden_warte(f : u64) -> u32
    effects { pure } costs <= 100000 ops;

-- -- the run-time `start`, which is a different thread ------------------------
--
-- A declared `concurrent` member is started once by the driver, before the
-- program runs; a `start { f };` STATEMENT is executed by a running Gabbro
-- function, on a stack the EMITTER laid out as a static region of the unit. So
-- these two take a stack top and a join word where the pair above takes a blob
-- the runtime owns (`laufzeit/bindung.h` says why).
--
-- **This is where the raw system call lives**, and it is the last one: `clone`
-- (56) on the handed stack, the thread's own `exit` (60) when the root returns,
-- and `futex` (202) for the wait. They leave no undefined symbol at all, which
-- is why `instrumente/pruefe-os-bindung.sh` counts SITES for them
-- (`MARKE_ROHRUF`) and not names -- a runtime that had hidden its Linux
-- dependency in assembly would pass a symbol stage untouched. The mark is 0 in
-- `laufzeit/` since these two bodies exist.
extern fn gabbro_os_klon(koerper : u64, spitze : u64, wort : u64) -> u32
    effects { pure } costs <= 100000 ops;

extern fn gabbro_os_wort_warte(wort : u64, erwartet : u32)
    effects { pure } costs <= 100000 ops;

}
